    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "owe Property are delighted to bring to the market 242 Blarney Street, a charming three-bedroom detached residence ideally positioned in one of Cork City's most established and convenient locations. Dating from circa 1900, this delightful home combines the character and charm associated with a property of its era with the comfort and convenience required for modern living. Extending to approximately 84 sq. m., the property has been lovingly maintained by its previous owner and is presented to the market in excellent condition throughout. Solar panels are installed for both electricity and water. One of the outstanding features of 242 Blarney Street is undoubtedly its location. Situated within easy reach of Cork City Centre, residents can enjoy an exceptional level of convenience, with an extensive range of shops, cafés, restaurants, bars, schools, colleges, workplaces and leisure facilities all close by. The property is also well positioned for access to the city's transport network, while the likes of UCC, MTU, CUH and Mercy University Hospital are all readily accessible. The surrounding area offers the very best of city living. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, condition and superb location of this attractive city residence."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Living Room:\r\n4.60m x 3.48m\r\nSpacious living room which benefits from tiled floor that flows throughout the entire downstairs accommodation. \r\n\r\n\r\nFamily Room/Bedroom\r\n4.25m x 2.16m \r\nLocated off the living room, this room can be either used as a bedroom or an additional living space\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen:\r\n4.14m x 2.95m \r\nFitted with sleek modern units, both floor and eye level. Benefits from integrated hob and double oven, dishwasher and washing \r\nmachine. \r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom: \r\n2.84m x 1.51m \r\nRecently renovated room, fully tiled and comprises of three-piece suite with shower cubicle and fitted with electric shower. \r\n\r\nLanding\r\n\r\nAccess to all bedroom accommodation and attic space via pull downstairs. \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1:\r\n3.33m x 2.32m \r\nDouble bedroom overlooking the front of the property, benefits from built in wardrobes. \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\r\n2.96m x 2.27m \r\nOverlooking the front of the property, the room benefits from built in wardrobes. \r\n\r\n\r\nOffice\r\n3.36m x 2.12m \r\nSpacious room located at the rear of the property, benefits from a  Velux window and timber floor. \r\n\r\n\r\nGarden:\r\nA courtyard to the rear of the property offers great privacy with mature shrubs and hedging, benefits from a garden shed offering great storage."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming three-bedroom detached home\r\nExcellent condition, blending period character with modern comfort.\r\nSuperb location close to Cork City Centre \r\nSolar panels provide electricity and hot water \r\nAll mains services\r\nGas fired central heating"
      },
